# Manual API tests for the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
# Start RestaurantApplication first, then run the requests from top to bottom
# (click the green arrow next to each request).
#
# The database starts with demo data (src/main/resources/db/seed/V100__demo_data.sql):
#   tables     id 1 = no. 1 (2 seats), id 2 = no. 2 (4 seats), id 3 = no. 3 (8 seats), id 4 = no. 5 (4 seats)
#   menu       id 1 Tripe Soup, id 2 Cabbage Rolls with Polenta, id 3 Papanasi, id 4 Lemonade (unavailable)
#   reservation id 1: Maria Ionescu, table no. 3, 2030-12-20 19:00
#   order      id 1: table no. 5, NEW, 2 x Tripe Soup + 1 x Papanasi = 70.00
# Ids assume a fresh database; reset it with: docker compose down -v

### 1. The whole menu / filtered by category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/menu

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/menu?category=DESSERT

### 2. Add a table -> 201 (id 5)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tables
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": 4, "seats": 6 }

### 3. Add a menu item -> 201 (id 5)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Grilled Mici", "category": "MAIN_COURSE", "price": 32.00, "available": true }

### 4. Update a menu item (Papanasi)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/menu/3
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Papanasi", "category": "DESSERT", "price": 27.50, "available": true }

### 5. Reservation at table no. 2 -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Andrei Popescu", "phone": "0722123456", "tableId": 2, "dateTime": "2030-12-20T19:00:00", "partySize": 4 }

### 6. Overlapping reservation at table no. 3 (Maria Ionescu has it at 19:00) -> 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "Elena Dobre", "phone": "0744555666", "tableId": 3, "dateTime": "2030-12-20T20:00:00", "partySize": 2 }

### 7. Order at table no. 5: 2 x Grilled Mici + 1 x Papanasi -> 201, total computed by the server
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tableId": 4, "items": [ { "menuItemId": 5, "quantity": 2 }, { "menuItemId": 3, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### 8. An unavailable item (Lemonade) cannot be ordered -> 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tableId": 4, "items": [ { "menuItemId": 4, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### 9. Order lifecycle: NEW -> IN_PREPARATION
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "IN_PREPARATION" }

### 10. Forbidden transition (back to NEW) -> 409
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "NEW" }

### 11. Orders by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders?status=IN_PREPARATION

### 12. A menu item used in orders cannot be deleted -> 409
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/menu/1

### 13. Invalid data -> 400 with one message per field
POST http://localhost:8080/api/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "price": -1 }
